From be47c5db34addeee2c3e3955c077b288235e701d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 13:13:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 61/64] hir_typeck: expand projections inside an associated
 type's own arguments

`expand_associated_types` normalised a `<T as Trait>::Item<..>` path's
self type and trait arguments, but never the arguments of the
associated item itself. A projection nested in a generic associated
type's argument list was left untouched when the outer projection
stayed opaque. nom 8.0.0's `Parser::process` (src/internal.rs) returns

    PResult<OM, Input, Self::Output, Self::Error>
    = Result<(I, <<OM as OutputMode>::Output as Mode>::Output<O>), ..>

and checking the `impl Parser<Input> for Choice<(A, B)>` (src/branch/mod.rs)
against it monomorphised `Self::Output` to
`<Choice<(A, B)> as Parser<Input>>::Output` inside `Mode::Output<..>`,
where it was never resolved to the impl's `Output`:

    error:0: Method process doesn't match trait:
    - Mismatched return type:
      Expected ..::Mode>::Output<<..::Choice<(A, B,),> as ..::Parser<Input,>>::Output/*?*/,>/*O*/
      Found    ..::Mode>::Output<Output/*I:1*/,>/*O*/

Expand the item's arguments along with the trait's, inside the same
recursion guard.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/hir_typeck/static.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/hir_typeck/static.cpp b/src/hir_typeck/static.cpp
index c14f4bc2..d31737a5 100644
--- a/src/hir_typeck/static.cpp
+++ b/src/hir_typeck/static.cpp
@@ -1878,6 +1878,10 @@ bool StaticTraitResolve::expand_associated_types__UfcsKnown(const Span& sp, ::HI
     this->expand_associated_types_inner(sp, e2.type);
     for(auto& arg : e2.trait.m_params.m_types)
         this->expand_associated_types_inner(sp, arg);
+    // The item's own parameters (a GAT's arguments) can hold projections too, and an opaque result keeps them as-is
+    // - e.g. `<<OM as OutputMode>::Output as Mode>::Output<Self::Output>` in a trait method's return type (nom 8.0.0)
+    for(auto& arg : e2.params.m_types)
+        this->expand_associated_types_inner(sp, arg);
     s_recursion_level -= 1;
 
     DEBUG("Locating associated type for " << e.path);
